{"id":"word:hebrew:H3809","type":"word","title":"לָא","subtitle":"H3809 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"or even, neither, no(-ne, -r), (can-) not, as nothing, without.","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to לָא (H3809) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: adv.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 82 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"לָא (lâʼ) means or even, neither, no(-ne, -r), (can-) not, as nothing, without. First listed occurrence: Dan 2 5."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"לָא","transliteration":"lâʼ","pronunciation":"law","strong":"H3809","lemmaId":"hebrew:H3809","partOfSpeech":"adv","forms":["לָ֥א","לָ֣א","לָא","לָֽא","לָ֤א"],"morphs":[["ATn",67],["AC/Tn",11],["ATi/Tn",3],["AR/Tn",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"or even, neither, no(-ne, -r), (can-) not, as nothing, without.","usage":"or even, neither, no(-ne, -r), (can-) not, as nothing, without.","full":"H3809. la or lah II. לָהֵן conjunction except, but (from לָא and הֵן 'not if' (compare Hebrew לא אם Gen 24:38 ); so Nabataean and Egyptian Aramaic להן Cooke 217, 219, 241 S-C Pap. C 6, 7 +; lâinnî, however Soc Arab. Dial. see Marokko 44, Anm. 103; אִילָּהֵין ᵑ7 32:28 ; 43:3 and elsewhere); — 1 after a negative (= Biblical Hebrew אִם כִּי , q. v.): a. except Dan 2:11 ; 3:28 ; 6:6 ; 6:8 . b. but (German sondern ) Dan 2:30 . 2 without a negative: however, but Ezra 5:12 .","rootNote":"(Aramaic) or לָה ; (Aramaic) (Daniel 4:32), corresponding to 3808","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"Dan 2 5","keyReferences":["Dan 2 5","Dan 2 9","Dan 2 10","Dan 2 10","Dan 2 11","Dan 2 11","Dan 2 18","Dan 2 27"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":82,"occurrences":[{"reference":"Dan 2 5","book":"Dan","chapter":2,"verse":5,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לָ֤א","source":"hebrew","morph":"ATn"},{"reference":"Dan 2